{"kind":"stack","id":"s-reversible","title":"Reversible changes: dissolving, mixing and changes of state","theme":{"background":"#f4f9f4","foreground":"#1d3b1d","font":"Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-q","content":"Sugar dissolves in water. Can you get the sugar back?"},{"type":"button","id":"c1-a","label":"Yes, by evaporating the water","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"No, the sugar is gone for good","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-c","label":"Only if we add more sugar","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Dissolving"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"When a solid mixes into a liquid and seems to disappear, but it can be got back by evaporating the liquid."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-n","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"Which change can be reversed by cooling?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"Melting chocolate that has gone runny","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"Baking a cake in the oven","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"Burning a piece of paper","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"You mix sand and small stones together. Is this change reversible?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"Yes, we can pick the stones out again","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"No, the sand and stones are joined forever","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"No, mixing always makes a new substance","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-t","content":"Aoife has a cup of water and a spoon of salt. She wants to know if she can get the salt back. What should she do?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"Heat the water until it evaporates","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"Throw the water away","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"Aoife heats the water and the salt is left in the dish. The change was reversible."},{"type":"button","id":"c6-n","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"Aoife throws the water away and the salt is lost. She could have kept it by evaporating the water first."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-n","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-q","content":"Water turns into ice in the freezer. Is this reversible?"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a","label":"Yes, the ice melts back into water","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"No, ice can never become water again","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-c","label":"No, freezing changes the water into air","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-t","content":"Changes of state"},{"type":"text","id":"c9-e","content":"When a solid, liquid or gas changes into another state, for example melting or freezing. Many can be reversed."},{"type":"button","id":"c9-n","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"Which of these is a change that can NOT be easily reversed?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"Baking a cake","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"Melting butter","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"Dissolving salt in water","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"Well done! You finished the reversible changes stack."},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"Many changes, like dissolving, mixing and melting, can be reversed. Keep looking for them around you."}],"actions":[]}}
